The examples in this directory are described in the userguide.

NOTE: the cylinder? problems are in the b-tensor formulation, whereas the
cylinder_c? problems are in the c-tensor formulation (standard c or logc).

NOTE2: the cylinder?a problems are similar to the corresponding cylinder?
problems, however using element level pointwise rotation reinitialization.
This simplifies the code, but only BDF type time discretization is available.
Hence, no trapezoidal rule or theta-method.

Short description
-----------------

cylinder1, cylinder1a:

 Startup of flow around a cylinder for a Giesekus model using the b-tensor
 formulation. Explicit div tau term.
 Problem 1: Flow around a confined cylinder.
   Periodical boundary conditions.
   Stress-explicit formulation of the momentum balance.
 Problem 2: b tensor

cylinder2, cylinder2a:

 Startup of flow around a cylinder for a b-representation differential
 Giesekus model. Semi-implicit div tau term.
 Problem 1: Flow around a confined cylinder.
   Periodical boundary conditions.
   Stress-implicit formulation of the momentum balance.
 Problem 2: b tensor
 Problem 3: b*b^T projection

cylinder3, cylinder3a:

 (This a problem similar to cylinder1, but solved using fully-implicit
  with Newton-Raphson for the b-tensor equation).

 Startup of flow around a cylinder for a Giesekus model using the b-tensor
 formulation. Explicit div tau term.
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson for the b-tensor.
 Problem 1: Flow around a confined cylinder.
   Periodical boundary conditions.
   Stress-explicit formulation of the momentum balance.
 Problem 2: b tensor

cylinder4, cylinder4a:

 (This a problem similar to cylinder2, but solved using fully-implicit
  with Newton-Raphson for the b-tensor equation).

 Startup of flow around a cylinder for a b-representation differential
 Giesekus model. Semi-implicit div tau term.
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson for the b-tensor.
 Problem 1: Flow around a confined cylinder.
   Periodical boundary conditions.
   Stress-implicit formulation of the momentum balance.
 Problem 2: b tensor
 Problem 3: b*b^T projection

cylinder5, cylinder5a:

 Startup of flow around a cylinder for a b-representation differential
 Giesekus model. 
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson
 Periodical boundary conditions.
 Compute drag on cylinder using reaction forces.
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.

cylinder6, cylinder6a:

 (This a problem similar to cylinder5, but now optionally zero blocks excluded)

 Startup of flow around a cylinder for a b-representation differential
 Giesekus model. 
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson
 Periodical boundary conditions.
 Compute drag on cylinder using reaction forces.
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally exclude certain zero blocks from the sparse matrix.

cylinder7

 (This a problem similar to cylinder6a, but now with a final steady state step)

 Startup + steady state of flow around a cylinder for a b-representation
 differential Giesekus model.
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson.
 After the final time step do a iteration to steady-state with Newton-Raphson
 Periodical boundary conditions.
 Compute drag on cylinder using reaction forces.
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally discard certain zero blocks from the sparse matrix.

cylinder8

 Sequence of steady states of flow around a cylinder for a b-representation
 differential Giesekus model.
 Iteration to steady-state with Newton-Raphson.
 Periodical boundary conditions.
 Compute drag on cylinder using reaction forces.
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally discard certain zero blocks from the sparse matrix.

cylinder9

 (This a problem similar to cylinder6a, but now it requires metis5,
  uses an input file and a possibility to restart)

 Startup of flow around a cylinder for a b-representation differential
 Oldroyd-B or Giesekus model.
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson
 Periodical boundary conditions.
 Compute drag on cylinder using reaction forces.
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally restart from a previously saved solution.
 Optionally discard certain zero blocks from the sparse matrix.

cylinder10

 (This a problem similar to cylinder8, but now it requires metis5,
  uses an input file, optionally scale the velocity and a possibility
  to restart)

 Sequence of steady states of flow around a cylinder for a b-representation
 differential Oldroyd-B or Giesekus model.
 Iteration to steady-state with Newton-Raphson.
 Periodical boundary conditions.
 Compute drag on cylinder using reaction forces.
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally discard certain zero blocks from the sparse matrix.
 Optionally restart from a previously saved solution.
 Optionally scale previous solution to match newly imposed flow rate.

cylinder_c1:

 (This a problem similar to cylinder1, but solved using c/logc)

 Startup of flow around a cylinder for a Giesekus model using the conformation
 tensor formulation. Explicit div tau term.
 Problem 1: Flow around a confined cylinder.
   Periodical boundary conditions.
   Stress-explicit formulation of the momentum balance.
 Problem 2: Conformation tensor

cylinder_c2:

 (This a problem similar to cylinder2, but solved using c/logc)

 Startup of flow around a cylinder for a Giesekus model using the conformation
 tensor formulation. Semi-implicit div tau term. 
 Problem 1: Flow around a confined cylinder.
   Periodical boundary conditions.
   Stress-implicit formulation of the momentum balance.
 Problem 2: Conformation tensor
 Problem 3: exp(s) projection

cylinder_c3:

 (This a problem similar to cylinder3, but solved using the c-tensor)

 Startup of flow around a cylinder for a Giesekus model using the conformation
 tensor formulation. Explicit div tau term.
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson for the conformation tensor.
 Problem 1: Flow around a confined cylinder.
   Periodical boundary conditions.
   Stress-explicit formulation of the momentum balance.
 Problem 2: Conformation tensor

cylinder_c4:

 (This a problem similar to cylinder4, but solved using the c-tensor)

 Startup of flow around a cylinder for a Giesekus model using the conformation
 tensor formulation. Semi-implicit div tau term.
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson for the conformation tensor.
 Problem 1: Flow around a confined cylinder.
   Periodical boundary conditions.
   Stress-implicit formulation of the momentum balance.
 Problem 2: Conformation tensor
 (Problem 3: exp(s) projection, logc not available with Newton-Raphson).

cylinder_c5:

 (This a problem similar to cylinder5, but solved using the c-tensor)

 Startup of flow around a cylinder for a Giesekus model using the conformation
 tensor formulation. 
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson
 Compute drag on cylinder using reaction forces.
 Periodical boundary conditions.
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.

cylinder_c6:

 (This a problem similar to cylinder6, but solved using the c-tensor)

 Startup of flow around a cylinder for a Giesekus model using the conformation
 tensor formulation. 
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson
 Periodical boundary conditions.
 Compute drag on cylinder using reaction forces.
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally exclude certain zero blocks from the sparse matrix.

cylinder_c7

 (This a problem similar to cylinder_c6, but now with a final steady state step)

 Startup + steady state of flow around a cylinder for a b-representation
 differential Giesekus model.
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson.
 After the final time step do a iteration to steady-state with Newton-Raphson
 Periodical boundary conditions.
 Compute drag on cylinder using reaction forces.
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally discard certain zero blocks from the sparse matrix.

cylinder_c8

 (This a problem similar to cylinder8, but solved using the c-tensor)

 Sequence of steady states of flow around a cylinder for a Giesekus model
 using the conformation tensor formulation.
 Iteration to steady-state with Newton-Raphson.
 Periodical boundary conditions.
 Compute drag on cylinder using reaction forces.
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally discard certain zero blocks from the sparse matrix.

cylinder_c9

 (This a problem similar to cylinder9, but solved using the c-tensor)

 Startup of flow around a cylinder for an Oldroyd-B or Giesekus model using
 the conformation tensor formulation.
 Fully-implicit with Newton-Raphson
 Periodical boundary conditions.
 Compute drag on cylinder using reaction forces.
 Optionally include Jacobian of SUPG test function.
 Optionally restart from a previously saved solution.
 Optionally discard certain zero blocks from the sparse matrix.

cylinder_c10

 (This a problem similar to cylinder10, but solved using the c-tensor)

 Sequence of steady states of flow around a cylinder for a b-representation
